# .scrub-secrets.local.example
#
# This is a template. The real file is named `.scrub-secrets.local`
# (no ".example"), lives at the repo root, and is gitignored — it is
# NEVER committed, and this example file must never contain real values.
#
# Purpose: scripts/scrub.sh reads .scrub-secrets.local (if present) as an
# extra, stronger local check on top of the regex patterns in
# scripts/scrub-patterns.txt. Put exact, known-bad literal strings here —
# one per line, plain text, no regex — for anything you know must never
# appear in a commit: a specific hostname, a specific username, a specific
# password or token you know was used in the source system, etc.
#
# To use it:
#   cp .scrub-secrets.local.example .scrub-secrets.local
#   # then edit .scrub-secrets.local and add real literal strings, one per line
#
# Lines starting with # are ignored. Blank lines are ignored.
#
# Example shape (these are NOT real values — replace before use):
# some-known-admin-username
# some-known-test-password
# some-internal-hostname.local
